  "_comment": "One run down the mountain, from the summit to the lodge, in three sections. The summit: off the line onto the glacier, a banked sweep round the shoulder, the cornice bends and a glide over the crevasse to the shelf below. The dam: a narrow road along the crest where the rockfall blocks one side then the other, then into the forest over the moguls, where the ice chute (a tunnel of ice with a dash strip out of it) cuts inside the bend and the avalanches pile snow on the road once the leader is through. The valley: the ski jump, a long glide down to the valley floor, the slalom through the ice gates, a banked last bend and the run to the lodge.",
